# Editor and merge debris. E0-12 made this reachable: `pyproject.toml` ships
# `app/ai/prompts/**/*` as package data, so any non-hidden file left in that
# directory is copied into the build context, packaged into the wheel, and
# installed into the runtime image. Before that entry the image held installed
# `.py` modules and nothing else. A `validity.v1.md~` or a `validity.v1.md.orig`
# is untracked, invisible in review, and sitting on the machine that runs
# `make docker-build` — so a key parked beside a prompt while debugging ends up
# in an image layer.
#
# The glob stays wide on purpose (ADR 0032: packaging decides what reaches
# production, the naming scheme decides what a file is called, and a glob that
# enforces the scheme does it by making files vanish from containers). This is
# the other end of that trade, and it is **this file's header warning applied in
# the direction that fails open**: a suffix nobody thought of is in the context
# until someone remembers to add it. It is the weaker half of the guarantee, and
# it is here rather than in the glob because narrowing the glob costs a silent
# production failure while missing a suffix costs a stray file.
backend/**/*~
backend/**/*.orig
backend/**/*.rej
backend/**/*.bak
